FerrionOS change to upstream userutils (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 641a5aa81574db79d883151bc3438d3e59f90b88 after the existing recipe patches.

When FERRION_LOGIN_SESSION=1 is set in the environment, login reads the session command from root-owned /etc/login-session.toml, checks claim_unlocked_session(None) before showing /etc/issue, opens /scheme/input/consumer as root, validates its display fpath prefix and VT number, activates its VT via /scheme/input/control and closes the control handle before spawning, prepares a verified 0700 /var/run/user/<uid> runtime directory and a fresh 0600 user-owned session.log created with O_EXCL after removing any existing name for stdout/stderr, applies /etc/login_schemes.toml, scrubs INIT_NOTIFY, TTY and stray non-CLOEXEC descriptors in 3..1024, spawns the session as the user with GSETTINGS_BACKEND=keyfile and FERRION_INPUT_CONSUMER_FD inherited, closes the parent's consumer handle, waits, restores the namespace, cleans stale top-level entries from /var/run/user/<uid> without following symlinks, and returns to the login VT.

